  "verbalization": "Mitomycin's relationship with UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 1-6 is supported by multiple pathways, all of which involve a common intermediate, 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid. This compound is identified as a target of both Patupilone and 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which in turn has a direct interaction with UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 1-6. The evidence suggests that mitomycin may act through a mechanism that indirectly targets this enzyme via these intermediates, possibly by modulating the activity of the intermediates or by influencing their downstream pathways. The shared involvement of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid across different targets highlights a potential regulatory or metabolic pathway that connects mitomycin to UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 1-6. The presence of multiple independent pathways reinforcing this relationship supports the hypothesis that mitomycin may exert its effects through a mechanism that involves these intermediates, potentially by affecting their expression or activity.",
